<title>FRANCE: GAN makes first-half loss due property.</title>
<headline>GAN makes first-half loss due property.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net consolidated loss			965  vs	     387</p>
<p>    Net preexceptional loss		    773  vs	     387</p>
<p>    Exceptional provision for CTR sale     192  vs	     --</p>
<p>    Property banking loss		    1,787  vs	   1,310</p>
<p>    Results excluding property banking   1,015  vs	     923</p>
<p>    Insurance profit				464  vs	    489</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>	Life assurance France		     425  vs	    627</p>
<p>	Non-life France		     loss  162  vs     loss 359</p>
<p>	Insurance, reinsurance abroad	   202  vs	    221</p>
<p>    CIC bank subsidiary			   472  vs	    387</p>
<p>    Other bank and financial units	     79  vs	     47</p>
<p>NOTE - GAN, whose CIC banking subsidiary is being privatised in preparation for the state insurer's own sell-off, said in its results statement that the first-half 1995 result included a 432 million franc exceptional gain from the activation of deferred life insurance contract acquisitions.</p>
<p>The property banking loss of 1,787 million francs comprises a loss of 799 million at its UIC unit versus 596 million last time round and a loss of 988 million tied to its defeasance plan versus 714 million francs at the same stage in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
